veryone out there to make life  prettier to make every day better  so uh kate uh will you  show us your dresser and how you  approached the challenge  teach us so dresser's right behind me uh  i miss going to flea markets so i wanted  to bring a little bit of that quirky  essence into this dresser i had some  left  paint um and some really sweet knobs and  just felt that i could add a little bit  of little details to this  you know simple dresser and you know  bring some bring some cork to it  i mean i feel kind of bad that we threw  you a curveball of the yellow in this  challenge and yet  i'm so glad that we did because i love  this pink trim  because i don't often see trim in the  actual drawer  it's always on the dresser itself that  is brilliant  i also love that you combine two  different knobs i feel like people would  be very scared of that  um but making that top drawer its own  little entity  brilliant i love it i love it  i absolutely am in awe i always am  learning stuff and this is what's so  exciting  trim on the drawer itself  okay carly you deconstructed  and then reconstructed your dresser wow  okay may we see it how did it come out  teach us  so i truly believe that necessity is the  mother of invention  and that's kind of what starts all of my  creative projects  and when i received the dresser i said i  need something in my dining room to hold  my liquor so i  took the legs off i decided to use  wooden dowels to kind of elevate it and  it truly elevated the whole entire piece  i love the way it came out  i am flabbergasted right now  because you i think are showing people  the mentality of what you see  is not necessarily what it needs to be  and that is so liberating and so freeing  it really does sometimes take someone  else to  open our own eyes and your execution is  beautiful  i love what mechanism did you put in  there may i ask to hold the glasses  upside down like what really reminds us  of being at a restaurant  yeah so you can buy these